# ChangeOrder Radar — frontend configuration.
# No secrets belong in this file or in source. The browser only ever holds
# public configuration; the preserved backend issues the session cookie.
#
# Exactly one runtime mode is selected at build time:
#
#   demo         (default)  Nothing below is set. Clearly labelled synthetic
#                           records. No network calls.
#
#   secure-link             VITE_SECURE_WORKSPACE_URL is set. The preserved
#                           ChangeOrder Radar workspace stays authoritative for
#                           sign-in, upload, deterministic analysis, evidence
#                           and findings. This app links out for every real
#                           action and holds no project data. No direct
#                           integration is claimed.
#
#   api                     BOTH VITE_API_BASE_URL and
#                           VITE_API_CONTRACT_VERSION=v1 are set. Uses the v1
#                           gateway adapter. Partial or mismatched config FAILS
#                           CLOSED back to secure-link or demo — it never
#                           silently issues live calls.

# Absolute https URL of the preserved secure ChangeOrder Radar workspace.
# http:// is only accepted for localhost during development.
VITE_SECURE_WORKSPACE_URL=

# Future gateway only. Requires the contract version below to be exactly "v1".
# The gateway must be same-origin (or cookie-credential capable with CORS
# credentials) so conventional session auth works; no API keys in the browser.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=
VITE_API_CONTRACT_VERSION=
